# bbm-plan keys — copy this file to `.env` next to `bbm_providers.json` and
# fill in the one variable your provider entry names in `env_key`. The skill
# sources it before every run. Never commit a filled .env.
#
# The route itself (endpoint, api_style, model) lives in
# `bbm_providers.json`, not here: `--provider NAME` reads the entry, and
# this file only supplies the key that entry points at.

# The example provider file's entries name these:
OPENAI_API_KEY=
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# An entry may name any variable in `env_key`; if your key already lives in
# one of the repo's own (BBM_OPENAI_API_KEY, BBM_CLAUDE_API_KEY,
# BBM_GOOGLE_GEMINI_KEY), point `env_key` at that name instead of copying
# the key to a second place.

# The codex route (`--model codex`) uses no key at all — `codex login`.
